## Summary {.unnumbered}

::: callout-note
## Today you learned

1.  Grouped data needs **multilevel models**; ignoring structure makes
    you overconfident.
2.  **Partial pooling** sits between one-average-for-all and
    a-separate-average-each.
3.  `(1 | group)` adds a **varying intercept** per group in `brms`.
4.  **Shrinkage** pulls small-sample groups toward the grand mean — and
    improves predictions.
5.  `sd(Intercept)` estimates **between-group spread**, itself a
    finding.
:::

